WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:01.480
- I'm here with Lisa Rinna.

00:00:01.480 --> 00:00:03.520
And on the line now is also Rainn Wilson.

00:00:03.520 --> 00:00:04.356
Give it up!

00:00:04.356 --> 00:00:07.090
(audience clapping and cheering)

00:00:07.090 --> 00:00:09.670
My next guest is a two-time Grammy winner,

00:00:09.670 --> 00:00:11.280
whose single "Old Town Road"

00:00:11.280 --> 00:00:13.960
shattered just about
every record last year.

00:00:13.960 --> 00:00:17.440
His new EP is called "The
Singin' Hills Sessions: Mojave,"

00:00:17.440 --> 00:00:18.400
it's out now.

00:00:18.400 --> 00:00:20.501
Give it up for Billy Ray Cyrus, everybody!

00:00:20.501 --> 00:00:23.905
(mellow country music)

00:00:23.905 --> 00:00:26.990
Yes, I like that little lick.

00:00:26.990 --> 00:00:28.355
What's up, man?

00:00:28.355 --> 00:00:29.640
- I'm good, how you doing?

00:00:29.640 --> 00:00:31.210
- I'm doing all right,
I'm doing all right.

00:00:31.210 --> 00:00:33.800
Well, when you were here in March,

00:00:33.800 --> 00:00:36.747
before the world decided to just turn,

00:00:36.747 --> 00:00:38.910
"Old Town Road" was 10 times platinum,

00:00:38.910 --> 00:00:41.270
and now it's 13 times platinum.

00:00:41.270 --> 00:00:43.200
Can you believe it hasn't slowed down?

00:00:43.200 --> 00:00:45.093
People love that song.

00:00:46.050 --> 00:00:47.220
- It's been crazy.

00:00:47.220 --> 00:00:48.053
And, you're right,

00:00:48.053 --> 00:00:50.200
referring back to the last time I saw you

00:00:50.200 --> 00:00:52.610
was the last little bit

00:00:52.610 --> 00:00:55.070
of normal that I recall.

00:00:55.070 --> 00:00:56.010
Everything after that...

00:00:56.010 --> 00:00:59.800
I left from your couch
and went and did a show

00:00:59.800 --> 00:01:04.529
with Neil Diamond and
Sammy Hagar in Las Vegas.

00:01:04.529 --> 00:01:06.580
And I caught a Southwest flight

00:01:06.580 --> 00:01:08.920
the next morning after
that back to Nashville.

00:01:08.920 --> 00:01:11.560
And by the time I landed
the whole world had changed.

00:01:11.560 --> 00:01:14.100
So at this moment to be back with you

00:01:14.100 --> 00:01:15.020
going full circle,

00:01:15.020 --> 00:01:17.760
and we're all starting brand new again.

00:01:17.760 --> 00:01:19.430
And you're right about "Old Town Road."

00:01:19.430 --> 00:01:21.940
I think that a lot of
people hear that song

00:01:21.940 --> 00:01:23.540
and go back to 2019.

00:01:23.540 --> 00:01:26.423
I know I do, I loved 2019.

00:01:27.870 --> 00:01:30.743
- Really any year other
than this one, but yeah.

00:01:33.260 --> 00:01:35.540
- This year I'm looking forward to 2021.

00:01:35.540 --> 00:01:37.724
- Amen, your mouth to God's ear.

00:01:37.724 --> 00:01:41.340
Is it true you got your
first iPhone this year?

00:01:41.340 --> 00:01:43.118
Is that a real thing?

00:01:43.118 --> 00:01:44.870
- Yeah.

00:01:44.870 --> 00:01:46.670
It's a bit embarrassing
to keep bringing it up.

00:01:46.670 --> 00:01:50.480
But, I'd been living like Fred Flintstone

00:01:50.480 --> 00:01:54.260
and realized that my mom was
living like "The Jetsons."

00:01:54.260 --> 00:01:56.210
And I go, "Man, I'm
scared to death of change,

00:01:56.210 --> 00:01:58.500
but I think I really need
to step up to the plate."

00:01:58.500 --> 00:02:01.420
And now that I have, it's
opened up a whole new world.

00:02:01.420 --> 00:02:04.760
I write all my songs now on my iPhone.

00:02:04.760 --> 00:02:06.130
It's quicker, it's better.

00:02:06.130 --> 00:02:07.830
You can put it in your pro tools.

00:02:07.830 --> 00:02:09.660
It's like I can't believe,

00:02:09.660 --> 00:02:11.090
but I'm scared to death of change.

00:02:11.090 --> 00:02:12.430
And sometimes that's like that.

00:02:12.430 --> 00:02:14.670
But change is the only thing

00:02:14.670 --> 00:02:16.807
I think you can really count on in life.

00:02:16.807 --> 00:02:18.680
And I should have embraced it earlier.

00:02:18.680 --> 00:02:21.280
I've sent a lot of
blurry pictures out there

00:02:21.280 --> 00:02:22.450
over the last 20 years.

00:02:22.450 --> 00:02:24.320
I got my first BlackBerry I think

00:02:24.320 --> 00:02:26.890
while we were doing "Hannah Montana."

00:02:26.890 --> 00:02:28.960
I think I remember taking
a picture with Lisa.

00:02:28.960 --> 00:02:29.800
How you doing, Lisa?

00:02:29.800 --> 00:02:31.750
- I'm great, Billy, how are you doing?

00:02:31.750 --> 00:02:32.583
It's great to see you.

00:02:32.583 --> 00:02:34.240
- I'm doing great, you too.

00:02:34.240 --> 00:02:36.020
We had fun on "Hannah Montana," didn't we?

00:02:36.020 --> 00:02:38.050
- We sure did.
- I love that.

00:02:38.050 --> 00:02:39.243
- We sure did, I'll never forget it.

00:02:39.243 --> 00:02:41.862
And you know how much I love Miley.

00:02:41.862 --> 00:02:45.280
- Yeah, well, actually speaking of Miley,

00:02:45.280 --> 00:02:48.310
this was one of my favorite
things I've heard recently.

00:02:48.310 --> 00:02:50.920
So she shared her experience with UFOs,

00:02:50.920 --> 00:02:52.560
which I do believe life is out there,

00:02:52.560 --> 00:02:54.790
but you've had a similar experience.

00:02:54.790 --> 00:02:55.793
I didn't know that.

00:02:56.980 --> 00:02:59.582
- Well, I don't talk about it
all that often to be honest.

00:02:59.582 --> 00:03:01.490
But, you know, that goes back

00:03:01.490 --> 00:03:04.350
to when I was a little boy
growing up in Kentucky,

00:03:04.350 --> 00:03:07.070
there was this place
back in the mountains.

00:03:07.070 --> 00:03:09.140
There's these big old
beach trees back there.

00:03:09.140 --> 00:03:12.480
And beach trees are are good
to carve on with a knife.

00:03:12.480 --> 00:03:14.780
And way back in the 1930s,

00:03:14.780 --> 00:03:17.270
a guy that lived back in the mountains

00:03:17.270 --> 00:03:18.830
had had this experience

00:03:18.830 --> 00:03:22.270
which he carved the pictures on a tree.

00:03:22.270 --> 00:03:23.860
I found them when I was a little boy

00:03:23.860 --> 00:03:25.670
and it was an old Model T Ford,

00:03:25.670 --> 00:03:28.447
and a saucer, and this
alien looking thing.

00:03:28.447 --> 00:03:29.760
And I started researching.

00:03:29.760 --> 00:03:30.760
And I go, "Wait, man.

00:03:30.760 --> 00:03:33.940
There was like an alien
invasion in Kentucky

00:03:33.940 --> 00:03:37.000
in the late 1930s, who knew about that?"

00:03:37.000 --> 00:03:38.800
Yeah, and so I kind of got,

00:03:38.800 --> 00:03:40.930
I don't know, fascinated
with it as a little boy.

00:03:40.930 --> 00:03:43.620
And then a couple of times,

00:03:43.620 --> 00:03:46.570
you know, throughout life,
I've seen some crazy stuff.

00:03:46.570 --> 00:03:50.260
Some of it I'm sure most of
it's probably explainable.

00:03:50.260 --> 00:03:51.700
But some of it I like...

00:03:51.700 --> 00:03:53.340
Hey, I took that picture!

00:03:53.340 --> 00:03:56.177
- [Kelly] He said, "Hey!" (laughs)

00:03:58.510 --> 00:03:59.650
- I remember that one right there.

00:03:59.650 --> 00:04:01.733
That's a beauty, I took that.

00:04:01.733 --> 00:04:03.177
With my BlackBerry

00:04:03.177 --> 00:04:05.737
- With my BlackBerry, iPhone (laughs).

00:04:07.070 --> 00:04:08.850
So wait, Rainn and Lisa, do y'all believe,

00:04:08.850 --> 00:04:10.530
do you believe, Lisa,
in extraterrestrials?

00:04:10.530 --> 00:04:11.699
- I do.
- I do too.

00:04:11.699 --> 00:04:13.115
I don't I think it's what we think it is.

00:04:13.115 --> 00:04:14.060
- I know.
- But I do believe

00:04:14.060 --> 00:04:15.170
in like other life.

00:04:15.170 --> 00:04:17.600
- I think that we can't be the only life.

00:04:17.600 --> 00:04:19.080
- I think that's so egocentric to think.

00:04:19.080 --> 00:04:20.220
- I think so too, right?
- Yeah.

00:04:20.220 --> 00:04:21.480
- I mean unless you don't believe in it,

00:04:21.480 --> 00:04:23.280
and then I think that's fine, Rainn.

00:04:24.880 --> 00:04:25.713
- No, no.

00:04:25.713 --> 00:04:29.420
Oh, I totally believe that there's aliens

00:04:29.420 --> 00:04:30.630
and some kind of,

00:04:30.630 --> 00:04:33.080
they'd be traveling and
they'd be observing us.

00:04:33.080 --> 00:04:34.670
And right now I think those aliens

00:04:34.670 --> 00:04:37.070
are looking down on
planet Earth and going.

00:04:37.070 --> 00:04:40.550
- [Lisa] Yes, I would agree.

00:04:40.550 --> 00:04:41.780
- They're behind the curve.

00:04:41.780 --> 00:04:43.403
They just can't figure it out.

00:04:44.430 --> 00:04:45.730
All right, well, Billy Ray,

00:04:45.730 --> 00:04:48.350
later you will be performing
a cover from your new album.

00:04:48.350 --> 00:04:50.320
So what is it and why did you record it?

00:04:50.320 --> 00:04:52.793
- Well the song is a LL Cool J song.

00:04:52.793 --> 00:04:55.017
It's called "Mama Gonna Knock You Out."

00:04:55.017 --> 00:04:57.363
- [Lisa] I love that song.

00:04:57.363 --> 00:05:00.620
- I played ball, I was a boxer,
and football, and baseball.

00:05:00.620 --> 00:05:02.947
And my dad always had
this saying, he'd say,

00:05:02.947 --> 00:05:05.700
"Son, when you knock 'em out,
you don't need no judge."

00:05:05.700 --> 00:05:07.640
When you knock 'em out,
you don't need a judge,

00:05:07.640 --> 00:05:10.470
that means you can't get
cheated by the referees.

00:05:10.470 --> 00:05:14.270
And it was odd when we
started making this album

00:05:14.270 --> 00:05:16.830
we started messing around
with this LL Cool J song,

00:05:16.830 --> 00:05:18.550
and it just felt so fun.

00:05:18.550 --> 00:05:22.910
And it was great to
take that hip hop track

00:05:22.910 --> 00:05:25.380
and just turn it into somewhat of,

00:05:25.380 --> 00:05:26.910
we call this album Mojave,

00:05:26.910 --> 00:05:29.260
'cause we kind of stumbled
onto our own sound

00:05:29.260 --> 00:05:31.500
of a mixture of country, southern rock,

00:05:31.500 --> 00:05:34.090
blues, hip hop, rock and roll.

00:05:34.090 --> 00:05:35.320
It's a little bit of everything.

00:05:35.320 --> 00:05:37.230
And we call it the Mojave sound.

00:05:37.230 --> 00:05:39.900
And we took "Mama Gonna
Knock You Out" to the Mojave.

00:05:39.900 --> 00:05:43.320
And it's a lot of fun
to play, a lot of fun.

00:05:43.320 --> 00:05:45.910
I'm looking forward to
when this pandemic's over

00:05:45.910 --> 00:05:47.390
and we can get back to the real life

00:05:47.390 --> 00:05:48.980
and take the music out on the road.

00:05:48.980 --> 00:05:50.540
And see the people

00:05:50.540 --> 00:05:52.220
and everybody celebrate through the music,

00:05:52.220 --> 00:05:54.220
and sing and dance, and love one another.

00:05:54.220 --> 00:05:57.490
- Yeah, oh man, I miss
shows, I'm with you.

00:05:57.490 --> 00:05:59.410
Well, members from my band, y'all,

00:05:59.410 --> 00:06:01.010
actually worked on this EP with you.

00:06:01.010 --> 00:06:02.900
You wanna give 'em a shout out right now?

00:06:02.900 --> 00:06:04.681
- What's up, Jaco?

00:06:04.681 --> 00:06:06.790
- Jaco, you played on it?

00:06:06.790 --> 00:06:07.623
I didn't know.

00:06:07.623 --> 00:06:08.770
- He's a producer.

00:06:08.770 --> 00:06:12.650
- What? You were so quiet and humble.

00:06:12.650 --> 00:06:15.650
You didn't mention that at all.

00:06:15.650 --> 00:06:17.060
- It's not out yet, right?

00:06:17.060 --> 00:06:18.137
- Well, okay.

00:06:18.137 --> 00:06:20.420
I'm like okay, Mr. Producer Man.

00:06:20.420 --> 00:06:22.310
I didn't know that.

00:06:22.310 --> 00:06:24.030
I always knew you were a bad ass musician,

00:06:24.030 --> 00:06:26.220
I didn't know you did
that, that's amazing.

00:06:26.220 --> 00:06:28.140
Get it, Jaco.

00:06:28.140 --> 00:06:30.557
All right, well Billy
Ray's new album is called

00:06:30.557 --> 00:06:32.460
"The Singin' Hills Sessions: Mojave,"

00:06:32.460 --> 00:06:33.710
and you can buy it today.

